   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "regbound1",
    "number": "Theorem (regbound1)",
    "quote": "Choose as algorithm parameters \n\\begin{equation}\\label{banditalgoparams}\nC=4194304K^6\\rho^3\\omega^2 \\alpha^2\\exp{(16\\alpha)} / \\delta^2, \\quad \\lambda = 8\\sqrt{\\frac{\\rho K}{Crmn}}.\n\\end{equation}\n\nThen the regret of $\\pi_\\text{nuc-norm}(C,\\,\\lambda)$\nsatisfies\n\\begin{align*}\n\\op{Regret}\\prns{T;\\pi_\\text{nuc-norm}(C,\\,\\lambda)}&\\leq ((Cr(m+n)+3)\\log(T)+1)\\omega\n\\\\&=O\\prns{r\\max(m,n)\\log(T)}\n\\end{align*}\nfor all $T\\leq (m+n)^{\\frac{mn}{C(m+n)}r}$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Paper's m (types) -> M_ctx, n (items) -> n_items, K (assortment size) -> canonical m, r -> r_rank. Regret is defined as difference of expected cumulative rewards vs the Theta*-greedy policy, i.e. pseudo-regret vs best assortment per context. Algorithm does not need T, so anytime, but bound valid only for T below a threshold."
  },
